stateDiagram-v2
    accTitle: Login authorization and vault locking
    accDescr: For an enrolled vault, signed-out access requires the Master Password and current OTP. A fixed five-hour login contains shorter vault-open windows, table lock, temporary desktop actions and a Windows lifecycle lock. Reopening needs the Master Password without extending login. Table lock preserves cached metadata; lifecycle lock clears it. Temporary actions relock on success or failure. Logout, expiry and process exit end authorization.
    direction TB
    state "Signed out: no login or DEK" as signedOut
    [*] --> signedOut
    state "Active login: fixed five-hour maximum" as login {
        state "Unlocked: DEK and data in memory" as unlocked
        state "Table locked: cached metadata retained" as tableLocked
        state "Temporary desktop action" as oneAction
        state "Lifecycle locked: workspace cache cleared" as screenLocked
        [*] --> unlocked
        unlocked --> tableLocked: Manual lock or fixed vault deadline
        tableLocked --> unlocked: Unlock vault + correct Master Password
        tableLocked --> oneAction: Protected action + correct Master Password
        oneAction --> tableLocked: finally relock on success or failure
        unlocked --> screenLocked: Windows lock, disconnect, suspend or resume
        tableLocked --> screenLocked: Windows lifecycle event
        oneAction --> screenLocked: Windows event cancels action
        screenLocked --> unlocked: Correct Master Password during same login
    }
    signedOut --> login: Master Password + current Authenticator code
    login --> signedOut: Logout, login expiry or app exit
